Z||000013||bubbajoexx||01-09-2001||08:55 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Archie:<BR>[B]I designed an adapter system for the GN back in 1991.<P>no need for adapters if you use the right block<BR>sorry arch no flame intened but I believe that if you are going to spend 3000 on a gnx engine you should install the set up with out an adapter changing to the front drive 85 block is easy and every thing fits because the 85 block still used the dist with the fuel injection system so the transfer of parts is easy.<P> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by bubbajoexx (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000014||Archie||01-09-2001||10:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bubbajoexx:<BR><B><BR>no need for adapters if you use the right block<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That may be the case Bubba...... BUT the guy who started this thread asked about the GN engine, AND Someone, before you, already mentioned that you can use the FWD block.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||01-09-2001||11:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B> <BR>Archie,<BR> Are you still making those adapters, or was that just a one time thing?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I still make them up once in a while for special orders. When someone orders one, I make up 5 or 6 and carry them in stock for as long as they last. Have only sold like 12 or 14 thru the years. I also sold a couple of the adapter systems to D&R. I never really tried to market the GN kit. Although it cost me a small fortune to do the R&D on the GN kits, I remained unconvinced that the GN was a better choice than the SBC. As I've said before, I really don't want to sell something to people that I wouldn't use myself.<P>Archie||||reg||1
