Z||000018||hugh||01-10-2001||09:56 PM||||I just spent about 15 minutes on a post for this thread and lost it somehow.Here is a condensed version.1st-GNX parts are for someone with very deep pockets.2nd-400hp is just about the upper limits because of only 4 head bolts per cylinder.3rd-84/85 intake manifolds have their inlets at the rear of the block and have larger throttlebodies than the later intercooled 86/87's. 4th-The 3.8front wheel drive is an offcenter engine.If the front wheel engine is an on center engine,the manifold will not fit. <p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
